          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "Several Brisbane-based and Brisbane-present consultancies specialise in **Microsoft Copilot Studio**, **AI agent development**, and **practical workflow automation** (typically through the Microsoft Power Platform and Azure AI stack). \n\nBecause mid-market businesses usually need practical ROI and governance—rather than bloated advisory decks or purely speculative pilots—the landscape divides into two main categories: **local boutique AI/automation specialists** and **established Tier-1 Microsoft Solutions Partners**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Dedicated AI & Automation Boutiques (Brisbane-Headquartered)\n\nThese firms are generally the best fit for agile mid-market projects where you need hands-on practitioners who build inside your tenant without massive overhead:\n\n* **Frontrow Technology** (Queen St, Brisbane)  \n  * **Focus:** Senior Microsoft AI advisory and engineering led by Microsoft MVPs.  \n  * **Strengths:** They cut straight past generic chatbot pilots to build functional, production-ready AI agents using **Microsoft Copilot Studio** and **Azure AI Foundry**. They are well suited for mid-market leaders who want architecture, tenant governance, and custom agent logic done correctly from day one.\n* **Corporate Agents** (Brisbane HQ)  \n  * **Focus:** AI workflow automation and closing the \"pilot-to-production\" gap.  \n  * **Strengths:** Specifically targets mid-to-large businesses looking to automate complex, multi-step workflows. They specialize in building agents that read unstructured inputs (invoices, forms, messy customer emails) and execute actions across ERPs, CRMs, and Microsoft cloud environments.\n* **Connected Platforms** (Brisbane)  \n  * **Focus:** Practical Microsoft 365 automation for mid-market and SME clients.  \n  * **Strengths:** Excellent for businesses starting from scratch with workflow modernization. They focus on practical use cases: combining Power Automate, Microsoft 365 Copilot, and custom approval flows to remove repetitive admin before scaling up complexity.\n* **C9 (C9 Pty Ltd)** (Brisbane presence)  \n  * **Focus:** Low-code conversational AI and custom Copilot Studio extensions.  \n  * **Strengths:** Purpose-built Copilot Studio developers who build intelligent assistants connecting Microsoft 365 apps with external APIs and legacy business databases.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Tier-1 Microsoft Solutions Partners (Strong Mid-Market Practices)\n\nIf your mid-market business requires end-to-end support—including Microsoft licensing optimization, complex ERP (Business Central/Finance) integration, and formal change management:\n\n* **Barhead Solutions** (Queen St, Brisbane Office)  \n  * **Focus:** Power Platform, Dynamics 365, and Copilot Studio specialist.  \n  * **Strengths:** Widely recognized as one of Australia’s top Power Platform partners. They have been early movers in generative AI, routinely delivering **Copilot Studio custom agents** tied into CRM and operational backends. They offer quickstarts specifically designed for mid-market operational automation.\n* **Data#3** (HQ in Brisbane / Toowong)  \n  * **Focus:** National Microsoft powerhouse headquartered locally in Brisbane.  \n  * **Strengths:** While they handle the ASX top 100, their commercial/mid-market team handles large volumes of Microsoft Copilot readiness, security assessments, and Power Automate workflow designs. Best if you need large-scale licensing advisory coupled with Azure OpenAI / Copilot Studio services.\n* **Rapid Circle** (Brisbane Office)  \n  * **Focus:** Cloud, Modern Work, and Copilot AI Centre of Excellence.  \n  * **Strengths:** Built their Brisbane practice through the acquisitions of local stars *Adopt & Embrace* (user adoption/change experts) and *Insync Technology*. They excel at ensuring that automated agents built in Copilot Studio are actually adopted by operational staff, paired with rigorous data security frameworks.\n* **Professional Advantage** (Brisbane/QLD team)  \n  * **Focus:** Mid-market business applications and Power Platform automation.  \n  * **Strengths:** Dedicated Copilot Studio consulting packages aimed at automating structured tasks (finance matching, client intake triage, internal knowledge search) within Microsoft 365 and Dynamics.\n\n---\n\n### Suggested Selection Criteria for the Mid-Market\n\nWhen speaking with these providers, verify that they focus on **autonomous agents and automated flows**, not just Microsoft 365 Copilot license setup:\n\n1. **Copilot Studio vs. Standard Copilot:** Ensure they build *autonomous agent flows* inside **Copilot Studio** (using triggers, event-driven architecture, and custom connectors) rather than just teaching staff how to write prompts in Word/Teams.\n2. **Data & Security Boundary:** They should demonstrate how your internal business data stays within your Australian tenant boundary (Entra ID, RBAC, Data Loss Prevention policies).\n3. **Power Automate / API Handshake:** A practical agent should read data *and* take action (e.g., updating a record in Business Central, Xero, or Salesforce via Power Automate plugins). Ask them for a demonstration of a multi-step agent flow they’ve shipped.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
